<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n71904" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀβελ-ίας</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρτος, ὁ,</span>
		roll or loaf <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>baked</i> or
				<i>toasted on a spit,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Vict.</u>
				2.42
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				103
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.273
			</span></i>, cf. Moer.<i><span class="en">
				p.287
			</span></i> P. ; without <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρτος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pherecr.
				55
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nicopho
				15
			</span></i> :—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀβέλιος</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				<u>CIG</u>
				3597b
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Ilium</span>) ; and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀβελίτης</span></b>  (q. v.). But in
			<u>AB</u>III we have <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀβολίας
				ἄρτους: τοὐς ὀβολοῦ πωλουμένους, Ἀριστοφάνης
				Πελαργοῖς</span> (<i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				440
			</span></i>).— <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				3.111b
			</span></i> writes it <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀβελίας</span> and
			gives both interpretations.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
